1
00:01:28,224 --> 00:01:34,063
BATTING UP A STORM!

2
00:01:40,336 --> 00:01:42,205
This is Yuki Aikawa!

3
00:01:42,405 --> 00:01:44,007
I'm a big fan of hers!

4
00:01:44,507 --> 00:01:45,742
Well, let's see...

5
00:01:45,975 --> 00:01:50,213
She'll come to Kameari Shopping District for a charity concert in two weeks.

6
00:01:50,413 --> 00:01:53,383
Lucky! I'll get her autograph!

7
00:01:53,583 --> 00:01:56,586
-But Ryotsu, look at this. -Huh?

8
00:01:58,254 --> 00:01:59,889
Hmm, it says...

9
00:02:00,089 --> 00:02:03,292
Kameari South Shopping District is also doing a charity concert.

10
00:02:03,526 --> 00:02:04,360
Lucky!

11
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:07,830
What? She's coming there in two weeks too!

12
00:02:08,564 --> 00:02:10,099
What's going on!

13
00:02:10,299 --> 00:02:15,004
Looks like the agency made a mistake and double-booked it.

14
00:02:15,204 --> 00:02:19,709
The shopkeepers in the two shopping districts don't get along, do they?

15
00:02:19,909 --> 00:02:21,277
What are they gonna do?

16
00:02:21,477 --> 00:02:23,846
I heard they'll settle it with a baseball game.

17
00:02:24,247 --> 00:02:25,448
A baseball game?

18
00:02:25,648 --> 00:02:30,953
Come to think of it, the Kameari shopkeepers were practicing earlier.

19
00:02:31,187 --> 00:02:31,921
Eh?

20
00:02:41,030 --> 00:02:45,902
Well, I don't care who wins as long as I get to meet Yuki Aikawa.

21
00:02:46,335 --> 00:02:46,969
Oh!

22
00:02:47,203 --> 00:02:47,804
Eh?

23
00:02:48,471 --> 00:02:50,273
On no, no, no!

24
00:02:50,473 --> 00:02:54,277
I was so distracted by Yuki-chan I forgot to pre-order the game!

25
00:02:54,477 --> 00:02:56,412
Hurry up!

26
00:02:57,947 --> 00:03:00,316
"KAMEARI SOUTH SHOPPING DISTRICT"

27
00:03:02,118 --> 00:03:06,489
Hey! Is Campus Fairy Quest 2 still up for pre-order?

28
00:03:06,689 --> 00:03:08,324
-Welcome. -Huh?

29
00:03:09,492 --> 00:03:11,360
Oh! Kiyohara!

30
00:03:12,462 --> 00:03:14,263
Are you really Kiyohara?

31
00:03:14,464 --> 00:03:16,432
Why is a pro baseball player here?

32
00:03:17,300 --> 00:03:18,301
Actually...

33
00:03:18,501 --> 00:03:23,005
my son's classmate's father's business partner's company president's wife's

34
00:03:23,239 --> 00:03:29,312
granny's distant relatives played against Kiyohara when he was in Little League.

35
00:03:29,512 --> 00:03:32,448
That's why he's helping out at this store.

36
00:03:32,648 --> 00:03:35,551
Now he's a part of this shopping district.

37
00:03:35,918 --> 00:03:36,652
Yes!

38
00:03:36,853 --> 00:03:39,789
I'll do my best in the next game too.

39
00:03:39,989 --> 00:03:43,726
I see. If Kiyohara is playing, then you've already won.

40
00:03:43,960 --> 00:03:47,830
I'll cheer for you too, Chairman, so get me Yuki-chan's autograph!

41
00:03:48,030 --> 00:03:50,032
Sure, leave it to me!

42
00:03:51,367 --> 00:03:53,202
I'm counting on you!

43
00:03:55,271 --> 00:03:58,007
"OZAKI MODEL SHOP"

44
00:03:58,207 --> 00:03:59,842
What?!

45
00:04:00,042 --> 00:04:01,644
Kiyohara?!

46
00:04:01,844 --> 00:04:04,547
Yeah. He was the same guy I saw on TV.

47
00:04:04,747 --> 00:04:07,116
Damn Mizuhara! What a dirty trick!

48
00:04:07,316 --> 00:04:10,119
Bringing in a pro baseball player for a sandlot game!

49
00:04:10,753 --> 00:04:12,488
What are we gonna do, Ozaki-san?

50
00:04:12,688 --> 00:04:17,160
No matter how hard we practice, we can't beat a pro.

51
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:20,429
Fine! If they're bringing in a ringer, then so are we!

52
00:04:20,663 --> 00:04:24,534
We can't afford to lose this game, no matter what!

53
00:04:27,370 --> 00:04:30,573
But we don't even have anyone in mind.

54
00:04:30,773 --> 00:04:34,577
Isn't there anyone out there who's incredibly good at baseball?

55
00:04:40,149 --> 00:04:43,085
Hey! Give me back my lunch!

56
00:04:45,221 --> 00:04:46,222
Gimme your bike!

57
00:04:56,899 --> 00:04:57,934
Wait!

58
00:05:06,008 --> 00:05:07,743
What insane strength!

59
00:05:07,944 --> 00:05:11,480
With superhuman stamina and the vitality of a cockroach,

60
00:05:11,714 --> 00:05:14,617
the only one who can take on Kiyohara in this town is that man,

61
00:05:15,218 --> 00:05:17,119
Kankichi Ryotsu!

62
00:05:18,054 --> 00:05:20,356
Ah, just go home already!

63
00:05:23,225 --> 00:05:28,030
Ridiculous! Helping out in a sandlot game won't earn me a single yen!

64
00:05:28,631 --> 00:05:31,634
If we win, you'll get to see Yuki Aikawa up close.

65
00:05:31,834 --> 00:05:35,204
Even if South Shopping District wins, I'll get to see her.

66
00:05:36,038 --> 00:05:38,641
As expected, he won't agree that easily.

67
00:05:38,975 --> 00:05:40,977
No choice. Time for the secret weapon.

68
00:05:41,210 --> 00:05:42,245
"TOTAL DEBT 799,732 yen"

69
00:05:48,250 --> 00:05:51,120
That's your total debt owed to our shopping district.

70
00:05:51,520 --> 00:05:53,122
Time to pay up!

71
00:05:53,322 --> 00:05:57,259
That's dirty! You said you'd wait until my bonus!

72
00:05:58,327 --> 00:06:00,796
Hmm... did I?

73
00:06:00,997 --> 00:06:02,431
Pay up now!

74
00:06:04,267 --> 00:06:07,436
Come on!

75
00:06:08,638 --> 00:06:10,439
Come on! Come on!

76
00:06:11,140 --> 00:06:12,942
Come on! Come on! Come on!

77
00:06:13,409 --> 00:06:14,176
Come on!

78
00:06:14,644 --> 00:06:17,179
Okay, okay! I'll play!

79
00:06:17,413 --> 00:06:19,248
Oh, you'll do it?

80
00:06:21,083 --> 00:06:25,721
But if we win, you have to clear all my debts!

81
00:06:25,955 --> 00:06:27,089
That's the deal.

82
00:06:27,423 --> 00:06:29,325
Whaaat?!

83
00:06:30,559 --> 00:06:31,460
Let's say 20%.

84
00:06:31,661 --> 00:06:32,295
No way.

85
00:06:32,495 --> 00:06:33,162
Then 50%.

86
00:06:33,362 --> 00:06:34,163
Nope!

87
00:06:34,363 --> 00:06:35,164
80%!

88
00:06:35,364 --> 00:06:36,899
No, no, no!

89
00:06:37,133 --> 00:06:40,102
Ugh, fine! We'll cancel all of it!

90
00:06:40,303 --> 00:06:42,104
All right, deal!

91
00:06:42,705 --> 00:06:47,043
I can see now that you guys really care about rebuilding your shopping district!

92
00:06:47,276 --> 00:06:51,814
I may not be much, but let me lend a hand to Kameari Shopping District!

93
00:06:52,014 --> 00:06:54,116
To clear all his debts, huh...

94
00:06:59,989 --> 00:07:05,294
"KAMEARI SHOPPING DISTRICT VS. KAMEARI SOUTH SHOPPING DISTRICT."

95
00:07:05,761 --> 00:07:08,764
But why do I have to play too?

96
00:07:09,398 --> 00:07:13,335
I'm worried these shopping district guys don't have the stamina for this.

97
00:07:13,936 --> 00:07:16,305
I've never played baseball before...

98
00:07:17,039 --> 00:07:23,512
Now, we'll begin the Yuki Aikawa Cup, Kameari vs. Kameari South.

99
00:07:25,247 --> 00:07:29,018
&lt;i&gt;Top of the 1st inning.&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Kameari South coming up to bat.&lt;/i&gt;

100
00:07:29,785 --> 00:07:33,889
&lt;i&gt;Leading off, Sarashina Soba&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;delivery man, Carl Lewis.&lt;/i&gt;

101
00:07:40,863 --> 00:07:41,530
Come on!

102
00:07:41,731 --> 00:07:43,499
What?!

103
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:47,269
The track and field superstar, Carl Lewis!

104
00:07:47,703 --> 00:07:49,505
Kiyohara isn't the only one!

105
00:07:52,975 --> 00:08:00,049
Carl is the man my daughter's friend's acquaintance's cousin met online.

106
00:08:00,249 --> 00:08:02,051
Hey, c'mon, c'mon!

107
00:08:02,551 --> 00:08:06,255
&lt;i&gt;Fine, even if he's the best in the world&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;at the 100 meters and long jump,&lt;/i&gt;

108
00:08:06,455 --> 00:08:08,257
&lt;i&gt;he's still an amateur at baseball...&lt;/i&gt;

109
00:08:10,092 --> 00:08:11,594
&lt;i&gt;Probably!&lt;/i&gt;

110
00:08:16,065 --> 00:08:17,299
All right! Got him out!

111
00:08:18,134 --> 00:08:19,435
Heh heh, take that!

112
00:08:23,672 --> 00:08:24,440
Safe!

113
00:08:24,740 --> 00:08:26,909
Damn it!

114
00:08:27,443 --> 00:08:30,913
&lt;i&gt;Batting second, apprentice hairdresser,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;Kimiko Date.&lt;/i&gt;

115
00:08:31,814 --> 00:08:34,450
Now, it's a women's tennis star!

116
00:08:35,384 --> 00:08:38,087
I wonder if she's an acquaintance of Mizuhara-san too.

117
00:08:38,287 --> 00:08:39,922
How should I know!

118
00:08:40,389 --> 00:08:43,392
&lt;i&gt;Hmph! Like a tennis pro&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;could ever hit my pitch.&lt;/i&gt;

119
00:08:45,094 --> 00:08:46,495
&lt;i&gt;Take this!&lt;/i&gt;

120
00:08:52,835 --> 00:08:53,669
Safe!

121
00:08:55,237 --> 00:08:57,673
Nice! Keep it up!

122
00:08:59,608 --> 00:09:00,876
This time for sure!

123
00:09:02,411 --> 00:09:05,614
&lt;i&gt;Batting third, Sekiguchi Rice Shop&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;part-timer, Takanohana.&lt;/i&gt;

124
00:09:05,815 --> 00:09:07,183
Come on, Takanohana!

125
00:09:07,416 --> 00:09:09,418
What? There's more!

126
00:09:09,618 --> 00:09:11,787
Ryotsu, look!

127
00:09:11,987 --> 00:09:13,189
Whoa!

128
00:09:14,123 --> 00:09:15,624
That's pro soccer player Maezono!

129
00:09:15,825 --> 00:09:17,860
And pro basketball player Michael Jordan too!

130
00:09:18,060 --> 00:09:20,663
The others are all top sports players too!

131
00:09:21,197 --> 00:09:26,669
That's dirty! Using pros in a shopping district game is against the rules!

132
00:09:27,069 --> 00:09:28,737
Hmph! What are you talking about?

133
00:09:28,971 --> 00:09:33,075
Everyone in our team works in the shopping district.

134
00:09:33,309 --> 00:09:37,913
You're the one breaking the rules by using Ryo-san who's not even a shopkeeper!

135
00:09:38,280 --> 00:09:40,182
Grr... twisting logic like that...

136
00:09:41,050 --> 00:09:44,086
&lt;i&gt;Hmph! If that's how&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;you want to play it...&lt;/i&gt;

137
00:09:50,926 --> 00:09:53,629
&lt;i&gt;If I hit the ball into their bodies&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;and send them all off,&lt;/i&gt;

138
00:09:53,829 --> 00:09:55,064
&lt;i&gt;we'll win&lt;/i&gt;

139
00:09:56,065 --> 00:09:58,067
&lt;i&gt;by default!&lt;/i&gt;

140
00:09:58,934 --> 00:09:59,835
Yes!

141
00:10:01,737 --> 00:10:03,072
Hit by pitch!

142
00:10:03,506 --> 00:10:05,474
Oh no! That doesn't work at all.

143
00:10:05,674 --> 00:10:08,077
They practice bumping into each other every day.

144
00:10:09,411 --> 00:10:13,482
&lt;i&gt;Batting fourth, Mizuhara Toy Shop&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;part-timer, Kiyohara.&lt;/i&gt;

145
00:10:14,483 --> 00:10:19,021
&lt;i&gt;Sorry, Kiyohara,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;but your season's...&lt;/i&gt;

146
00:10:19,221 --> 00:10:21,190
&lt;i&gt;over!&lt;/i&gt;

147
00:10:23,192 --> 00:10:26,095
&lt;i&gt;A pitch like that won't work on a pro!&lt;/i&gt;

148
00:10:35,137 --> 00:10:38,140
&lt;i&gt;Grr... Fine! I'm going all out!&lt;/i&gt;

149
00:10:52,388 --> 00:10:56,225
Damn it! This is the first time I've allowed so many runs in one inning!

150
00:10:56,926 --> 00:10:59,762
The gap in skill is way too big. Maybe we should give up...

151
00:10:59,962 --> 00:11:02,464
Don't be ridiculous! My debt is on the line!

152
00:11:02,698 --> 00:11:04,700
No way I'm giving up now!

153
00:11:04,900 --> 00:11:06,468
But Ryotsu...

154
00:11:07,002 --> 00:11:08,370
Look over there!

155
00:11:08,571 --> 00:11:09,171
Huh?

156
00:11:16,712 --> 00:11:18,647
It's Nomo from the Major Leagues!

157
00:11:18,847 --> 00:11:21,016
Whaaat?!

158
00:11:21,250 --> 00:11:23,252
Honda! Get on base even if it kills you!

159
00:11:23,452 --> 00:11:25,154
N-No way...

160
00:11:27,122 --> 00:11:28,257
Play ball!

161
00:11:35,297 --> 00:11:36,665
Strike!

162
00:11:36,865 --> 00:11:39,268
Hey! Swing the bat at least!

163
00:11:40,336 --> 00:11:43,772
Strike!

164
00:11:43,973 --> 00:11:45,641
Batter's out!

165
00:11:48,877 --> 00:11:49,645
Sorry...

166
00:11:49,845 --> 00:11:51,447
You really...

167
00:11:51,647 --> 00:11:54,516
Hey, Nomo! This isn't even a fair game!

168
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:56,852
Take it easy on them!

169
00:11:57,052 --> 00:11:57,886
Okay.

170
00:11:59,888 --> 00:12:00,856
Come on!

171
00:12:04,526 --> 00:12:05,861
&lt;i&gt;I can hit this one!&lt;/i&gt;

172
00:12:07,830 --> 00:12:09,298
Oh, right field single!

173
00:12:10,132 --> 00:12:11,133
Maezono!

174
00:12:15,504 --> 00:12:16,605
Out!

175
00:12:18,607 --> 00:12:21,076
Fine, then I'll do it myself!

176
00:12:24,446 --> 00:12:26,782
Yes! Home run!

177
00:12:29,318 --> 00:12:30,352
What!

178
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:33,822
That's Bubka, the pole vaulting legend!

179
00:12:34,023 --> 00:12:35,791
We're doomed...

180
00:12:35,991 --> 00:12:36,692
Out!

181
00:12:36,892 --> 00:12:39,028
Three outs! Switch sides!

182
00:12:46,035 --> 00:12:47,936
You gotta be kidding me!

183
00:13:23,839 --> 00:13:24,673
Safe!

184
00:13:24,873 --> 00:13:25,974
I made it!

185
00:13:41,457 --> 00:13:42,291
Huh?

186
00:13:43,058 --> 00:13:43,792
Oh?

187
00:13:47,463 --> 00:13:48,564
Rain?

188
00:13:50,299 --> 00:13:54,636
Hey, it's starting to rain, so let's call it a day.

189
00:13:55,571 --> 00:13:57,639
What? What about the game?

190
00:13:58,440 --> 00:14:00,442
Of course we win.

191
00:14:00,642 --> 00:14:03,278
We're up by 23 runs.

192
00:14:05,647 --> 00:14:08,150
Or can you turn the game around?

193
00:14:10,018 --> 00:14:11,954
Let's give up now.

194
00:14:12,354 --> 00:14:15,958
That's right. We'll have another chance to call Yuki-chan.

195
00:14:16,959 --> 00:14:17,793
This is bad.

196
00:14:17,993 --> 00:14:21,130
My dream of being debt-free is slipping away!

197
00:14:21,663 --> 00:14:24,433
Well then, let's call the game here...

198
00:14:24,633 --> 00:14:25,734
Hold it!

199
00:14:25,934 --> 00:14:27,936
The game's only halfway done!

200
00:14:28,137 --> 00:14:31,607
We're just starting to warm up!

201
00:14:31,807 --> 00:14:33,976
Ryo-san, I know how you feel, but...

202
00:14:34,176 --> 00:14:35,177
You guys!

203
00:14:35,377 --> 00:14:39,047
You said we couldn't afford to lose today's game!

204
00:14:39,915 --> 00:14:42,951
Is that how determined you are?

205
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:48,023
And you pro players over there!

206
00:14:48,690 --> 00:14:52,828
If you're running from a little rain, you can't call yourselves true athletes!

207
00:14:53,028 --> 00:14:56,799
A real pro fights on, no matter the conditions!

208
00:14:57,166 --> 00:15:00,636
What are you talking about? Think about the situation!

209
00:15:00,836 --> 00:15:02,838
It's all right, Mizuhara-san.

210
00:15:03,238 --> 00:15:05,541
We have our pride as pros too.

211
00:15:06,842 --> 00:15:09,344
Got it. Let's finish this.

212
00:15:09,545 --> 00:15:12,714
Hmph! Don't you dare call it off no matter what!

213
00:15:16,051 --> 00:15:18,253
But even if we keep going...

214
00:15:18,487 --> 00:15:20,422
No, knowing Ryotsu,

215
00:15:20,823 --> 00:15:23,058
he might have a plan.

216
00:15:25,327 --> 00:15:28,897
&lt;i&gt;If the conditions get worse,&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;that just works in our favor.&lt;/i&gt;

217
00:15:40,209 --> 00:15:42,077
No holding back!

218
00:15:42,277 --> 00:15:44,580
Finish the game quickly!

219
00:15:45,347 --> 00:15:47,115
Okay, I get it.

220
00:15:51,353 --> 00:15:53,755
&lt;i&gt;But I can't see clearly...&lt;/i&gt;

221
00:15:58,694 --> 00:15:59,862
D-Darn it!

222
00:16:05,234 --> 00:16:07,302
Oh! My hand slipped!

223
00:16:11,206 --> 00:16:12,608
That was...

224
00:16:13,075 --> 00:16:15,010
On purpose, of course.

225
00:16:15,210 --> 00:16:17,479
He's already showing his true skills

226
00:16:18,947 --> 00:16:20,015
Where's the ball?

227
00:16:20,215 --> 00:16:23,619
Heh! Now's my chance.

228
00:16:23,852 --> 00:16:25,687
Round the bases!

229
00:16:25,888 --> 00:16:28,290
Yeah! We got a run back!

230
00:16:34,863 --> 00:16:36,698
I won't allow you another run!

231
00:16:37,332 --> 00:16:37,966
Come on!

232
00:16:43,972 --> 00:16:45,474
A Mirage Pitch?!

233
00:16:46,508 --> 00:16:49,278
Strike! Batter's out!

234
00:16:49,478 --> 00:16:52,981
That's dirty! You threw mud along with the ball!

235
00:16:53,315 --> 00:16:56,485
Hmph! Got any proof I did it on purpose?

236
00:16:57,119 --> 00:16:59,254
Sorry, Kiyohara. I didn't mean to,

237
00:16:59,454 --> 00:17:02,491
but this rain made my hand muddy.

238
00:17:02,724 --> 00:17:03,725
Forgive me.

239
00:17:04,192 --> 00:17:07,763
Yeah! We're both in bad conditions.

240
00:17:10,499 --> 00:17:15,203
Ryotsu really comes alive in situations like this...

241
00:17:21,376 --> 00:17:23,111
Oh, no! An infield hit!

242
00:17:25,914 --> 00:17:27,816
Easy run to second base!

243
00:17:30,519 --> 00:17:32,020
Tag out!

244
00:17:39,361 --> 00:17:44,833
&lt;i&gt;Heavy rain, strong winds, lightning and flood warnings were just issued for Tokyo.&lt;/i&gt;

245
00:17:45,033 --> 00:17:49,171
&lt;i&gt;Especially residents near rivers, please stay alert.&lt;/i&gt;

246
00:17:49,371 --> 00:17:51,707
We're facing a real disaster threat now.

247
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:52,808
Yeah.

248
00:17:53,008 --> 00:17:55,644
The Katsushika Police Emergency HQ just contacted us.

249
00:17:55,844 --> 00:17:59,514
Terai, Reiko, advise all riverside residents to evacuate immediately.

250
00:17:59,715 --> 00:18:00,349
Yes, sir!

251
00:18:02,784 --> 00:18:07,356
&lt;i&gt;Heavy rain, strong winds, lightning and&lt;/i&gt; &lt;i&gt;flood warnings have just been issued.&lt;/i&gt;

252
00:18:07,856 --> 00:18:12,527
&lt;i&gt;All residents near the river, evacuate to your designated shelter!&lt;/i&gt;

253
00:18:17,499 --> 00:18:20,068
The river is overflowing!

254
00:18:20,869 --> 00:18:24,840
We can't continue the game any further! Let's end it!

255
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:28,343
Hmph! If you're okay with losing, we can end it!

256
00:18:28,977 --> 00:18:31,346
D-Don't say stupid things!

257
00:18:31,713 --> 00:18:33,882
We're still winning!

258
00:18:34,082 --> 00:18:36,218
But the flow of the game is on our side!

259
00:18:36,418 --> 00:18:39,354
We've closed the gap to just three runs!

260
00:18:39,855 --> 00:18:43,291
I told you we won't stop the game no matter what happens!

261
00:18:43,525 --> 00:18:46,027
We're playing to the end!

262
00:18:51,199 --> 00:18:54,202
Ryotsu! Honda-san and the others are getting swept away!

263
00:18:54,403 --> 00:18:55,203
Doesn't matter!

264
00:18:55,404 --> 00:18:58,173
We can still play, even if we're short a guy or two!

265
00:18:58,707 --> 00:18:59,441
Take this!

266
00:18:59,641 --> 00:19:02,477
My deadly water-slash pitch!

267
00:19:03,078 --> 00:19:05,781
Everyone, please remain calm and evacuate!

268
00:19:06,014 --> 00:19:06,848
Don't panic!

269
00:19:07,049 --> 00:19:08,717
Please calm down and evacuate!

270
00:19:08,917 --> 00:19:11,787
-Everyone, please calm down. -This way, this way!

271
00:19:12,020 --> 00:19:14,923
-Please remain calm and evacuate! -Calm down!

272
00:19:15,123 --> 00:19:16,024
Help!

273
00:19:16,558 --> 00:19:17,893
Oh! Honda-san!

274
00:19:18,093 --> 00:19:19,261
He's getting swept away!

275
00:19:19,461 --> 00:19:21,797
Somebody help!

276
00:19:25,033 --> 00:19:26,268
I'm safe...

277
00:19:26,468 --> 00:19:27,502
You okay, Honda-san?

278
00:19:28,870 --> 00:19:33,041
Yeah, I got swept away during the top of the 8th inning.

279
00:19:33,308 --> 00:19:35,811
What? Are they still playing baseball?!

280
00:19:36,044 --> 00:19:37,679
Help!

281
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:41,116
What a bunch of idiots...

282
00:19:41,316 --> 00:19:42,617
Whoa! Ahh!

283
00:19:42,818 --> 00:19:44,453
H-Help!

284
00:19:49,991 --> 00:19:52,794
Now's my chance for a swimming home run!

285
00:19:52,994 --> 00:19:54,296
Iwasaki-san, please!

286
00:19:54,496 --> 00:19:55,430
Yes!

287
00:19:58,233 --> 00:20:00,001
Gah! Iwasaki, Women's swimming champ!

288
00:20:02,103 --> 00:20:03,505
I got it!

289
00:20:04,706 --> 00:20:07,275
Oh no!

290
00:20:16,785 --> 00:20:18,720
Yay! It's a tie!

291
00:20:18,954 --> 00:20:20,622
Ryo-chan!

292
00:20:21,323 --> 00:20:24,626
It's dangerous there! Evacuate now!

293
00:20:24,826 --> 00:20:27,963
Are you kidding? We've just tied the game!

294
00:20:28,163 --> 00:20:29,965
We can't stop now!

295
00:20:30,499 --> 00:20:31,132
Huh?

296
00:20:33,201 --> 00:20:34,336
Help!

297
00:20:37,138 --> 00:20:39,741
Without the pitcher, that's our win!

298
00:20:39,975 --> 00:20:41,343
I'm still here!

299
00:20:41,543 --> 00:20:42,177
What?

300
00:20:44,813 --> 00:20:47,716
I pitched back in high school!

301
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:50,685
I knew you'd show up, Kiyohara!

302
00:21:10,605 --> 00:21:12,674
Fine, just do whatever you want!

303
00:21:13,208 --> 00:21:16,711
This is all your fault for saying we'd settle it with baseball!

304
00:21:16,912 --> 00:21:18,680
You're the one who suggested it!

305
00:21:20,215 --> 00:21:21,183
I'm safe!

306
00:21:22,017 --> 00:21:23,985
-Are you okay? -Yeah, somehow...

307
00:21:24,386 --> 00:21:25,921
Let go! Hey, let go!

308
00:21:26,154 --> 00:21:28,690
Hey! The two managers are getting swept away!

309
00:21:28,890 --> 00:21:30,425
Hurry and help them!

310
00:21:30,992 --> 00:21:32,627
They're still arguing...

311
00:21:32,861 --> 00:21:34,863
So, what happened to the game?

312
00:21:35,063 --> 00:21:36,198
No idea...

313
00:21:40,368 --> 00:21:41,636
Ryo-chan...

314
00:21:49,644 --> 00:21:50,812
Here we go!

315
00:21:57,919 --> 00:21:58,820
Bring it on!

316
00:22:21,509 --> 00:22:24,145
Yay! Walk-off win!

317
00:22:35,690 --> 00:22:39,694
It's true! I really hit a walk-off homer!

318
00:22:40,228 --> 00:22:43,632
All right, all right. I believe you, Ryo-san.

319
00:22:44,065 --> 00:22:49,671
So it's decided Yuki Aikawa is coming to our Kameari Shopping District.

320
00:22:50,338 --> 00:22:54,809
Hold it! No one saw Ryo-san hit that home run!

321
00:22:55,343 --> 00:22:59,180
All the umpires got swept away in the top of the 9th.

322
00:22:59,781 --> 00:23:03,885
You! Are you saying you don't trust a police officer?

323
00:23:04,119 --> 00:23:08,023
You're the one who always says not to trust Ryo-san!

324
00:23:09,457 --> 00:23:12,794
Hey, my debt's canceled now, right?

325
00:23:17,632 --> 00:23:23,271
B-Bad news! Yesterday's storm kept Yuki-chan from getting back from her tour!

326
00:23:23,705 --> 00:23:24,739
What?!

327
00:23:24,973 --> 00:23:28,209
Then, today's event is...?

328
00:23:29,277 --> 00:23:31,212
Washed away, either way...

329
00:23:31,446 --> 00:23:32,047
Eh?!

330
00:23:32,747 --> 00:23:35,984
Well, let's go. Back to work, I guess.

331
00:23:36,685 --> 00:23:38,053
H-Hey! Wait up!

332
00:23:38,753 --> 00:23:42,190
So what about my debt?

333
00:23:42,390 --> 00:23:46,661
Ryo-san, sorry, but pretend this never happened.

334
00:23:47,462 --> 00:23:49,064
No way!

335
00:23:50,765 --> 00:23:58,306
At least give me 50% off my debt, or 20%, or even 10%!

336
00:24:03,178 --> 00:24:08,950
KANKICHI RYOTSU'S SHOCK MARRIAGE!
